      "imageWidth": 1708,
      "imageHeight": 1141,
      "story": "Charcoal burners is an 1886 painting by the Australian artist Tom Roberts. The painting depicts three rural labourers \"splitting and stacking timber for the preparation of charcoal\". Roberts, influenced by the Barbizon school and Jules Bastien-Lepage, would later return to the theme of rural men working in his works A break away! and Shearing the Rams.",
